  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-pillow-2026-112405",
  "summary": "Pillow: NULL pointer dereference in Image.merge via an unvalidated band 0",
  "details": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. From 12.0.0 until 13.0.0, Pillow's Image.merge() can dereference a null image8 plane. Validation skips the first input band, allowing a 32-bit integer or floating-point image backed by image32 storage to be merged as a narrower multiband image. A crafted IPTC file can reach this path when an application opens and loads it, or a caller can invoke Image.merge() directly with such a first band. This causes a native process crash. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0.",
